Rina (Docs): Quick micro-thread "; I'm putting together a one-line migration snippet for v1->v2 embeddings. Need: 1) tiny Python or TS example using model_id; 2) exact short error fragment for dim mismatch; 3) one-line changelog for console banner. Keep everything localizable.

Kevin (SDK): I'll paste a compact TS example you can copy:```ts
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RDW_KEY });
const map = { 'embed-old-512':'embed-new-768' };
const model_id = map['embed-old-512'] ?? 'embed-old-512';
const r = await c.embeddings.create({ model_id, input: ['hello'] });
console.log(r.data[0].embedding.length);
```

Mira (Runtime): Exact trimmed error payload: `{"error":"embedding failed: vector_dim 512 != expected 768","code":"ERR_DIM_MISMATCH"}`. For the doc use the fragment: "embedding failed: vector_dim". Also note: pin model version for deterministic vectors across rollouts.

Rina (Docs): Draft troubleshooting sentence for l10n: "If a 400 mentions 'vector_dim', verify model_id and remap or regenerate vectors; pin model versions for deterministic outputs." Priya  ok to localize?

Priya (L10n): Yes, one short sentence is fine. Please put it in the PR description.

Sam (PM): Changelog one-liner: "Embeddings: rename param to model_id (alias supported); ERR_DIM_MISMATCH on dim mismatch. See migration quickstart." Rina  add to banner.

Rina (Docs): Actions: Kevin add snippet + changelog to SDK PR; Mira add runtime test to assert "vector_dim" in 400; Priya queue localization on merge; Rina will open docs PR with the TS + troubleshooting sentence. Merge when green. :thumbsup: (End)
